{"chunk_id": "81babd7c2f94", "text": "In the Dandaka forest battle, the demon Khara and Rama exchange taunts amid their fierce duel. Khara, enraged, hurls a blazing mace that scorches the forest, but Rama shatters it mid\u2011air with arrows. Rama then mocks Khara\u2019s boasts, declaring that his death will free the forest from demonic terror and allow the sages to live without fear. Khara retaliates with insults and uproots a palm tree, hurling it like a weapon, yet Rama slices it apart and pierces him with countless arrows. Finally Rama releases a divine shaft given through the sage Agastya by Indra; it strikes Khara like a thunderbolt and kills him. The gods witness the feat and celebrate: Rama has slain fourteen thousand shape\u2011shifting demons along with Khara and Dushana, revealing his near\u2011divine prowess.\nRama and Khara exchange taunts; after destroying Khara\u2019s attacks, Rama kills him with a divine arrow, ending the demon assault in Dandaka.\nThemes: heroic combat, divine weapons, good versus evil, protection of sages, boast and retribution", "vector": [-0.0007271869108080864, -0.00933083239942789, 0.0007246677996590734, 0.00826944224536419, -0.013065853156149387, 0.007624546531587839, -0.03557673841714859, -0.02554055117070675, -0.03248661383986473, -0.011977591551840305, 0.011164754629135132, 0.013905560597777367, 0.0028852359391748905, 0.0024183583445847034, 0.004722516518086195, 0.008235854096710682, 0.037054624408483505, -0.019105030223727226, 0.022007061168551445, -0.018540747463703156, -0.0004379076126497239, 0.004924046341329813, -0.0043127392418682575, 0.020744141191244125, -0.029315877705812454, 0.02807982824742794, 0.025056879967451096, -0.024774737656116486, 0.009075561538338661, -0.006163455080240965, -0.003459596075117588, -0.02316249907016754, 0.007423016708344221, -0.016095519065856934, -0.02020672708749771, 0.002097589895129204, -0.0030431009363383055, -0.013361429795622826, 0.015181916765868664, 0.008618760854005814, -0.007611